  "notes": "U.S. Census Bureau Current Population Survey Annual Social and Economic Supplement (CPS ASEC) household money income series, 2000-2024. 'median' and 'mean' are national household money income in current dollars (Historical Table H-5, https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/cps/tables/time-series/historical-income-households/h05.xlsx). 'percentiles' p20/p40/p60/p80/p95 are upper income limits of each quintile / lower limit of top 5% from Historical Table H-1 (https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/cps/tables/time-series/historical-income-households/h01ar.xlsx); p50 duplicates the median. p10 and p90 are only available for 2023-2024 from the P60-286 report's Table A-3 (https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/demo/tables/p60/286/tableA3.xlsx) and are null for earlier years in this dataset (Census does not publish a consistent historical P10/P90 time series in the same table). 'gini' is the national Gini index from Historical Table H-4 (https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/cps/tables/time-series/historical-income-households/h04.xlsx). 'quintile_mean_income' (2000-2023) is mean income received within each quintile/top-5% group from Historical Table H-3 (https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/cps/tables/time-series/historical-income-households/h03ar.xlsx). 'quintile_shares_pct' and 'percentile_ratios' are only available for 2023-2024 from Table A-3 of the 'Income in the United States: 2024' report (P60-286). Income concept is CPS 'money income': pre-tax cash income including wages, self-employment, interest, dividends, rents, and cash transfers (Social Security, unemployment insurance, public assistance, etc.), but EXCLUDING capital gains, non-cash transfers (SNAP, Medicaid, employer health insurance), and taxes. This is closer to 'market'/pre-tax cash income than to a disposable-income concept; it is NOT equivalence-adjusted (equivalence-adjusted figures are separately published in Table A-3 but not included in this file's main series). All dollar figures are nominal (current-year) dollars unless noted."
